            <ArticleTitle>One Strike against Low-Carbohydrate Diets.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2015.07.022</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(15)00351-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is intense controversy over whether low-carbohydrate or low-fat diets are more efficacious for weight management. Using precise methodology, Hall et al. (2015) demonstrated that a low-carbohydrate diet promoted greater fat oxidation than an isocaloric low-fat diet but, in contrast to popular speculation, did not cause greater body fat loss.</AbstractText>
